Lota's Vulkan present patch, for Android alone: one statement of LÖVE's
src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp, inside #ifdef LOVE_ANDROID.
LÖVE creates its swap chain with an identity preTransform (line 2156),
and Android's loader returns VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR from vkQueuePresentKHR
whenever a swap chain's preTransform differs from the window's transform
hint, which on a phone whose display is portrait is a rotation in
landscape (frameworks/native vulkan/libvulkan/swapchain.cpp, in
QueuePresentKHR). Graphics::present rebuilds the swap chain on that result
(lines 643-650), and recreateSwapChain waits for the device to idle and
makes the swap chain's images and the depth and stencil image again
(lines 3685-3705), so in landscape it rebuilds every frame, and the game
runs at 20 to 30 frames a second where it runs at 60 in portrait. A new
swap chain has the same identity preTransform and gets the same result.
The image is presented even so: VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR is a success code, and
the compositor rotates the identity buffer, as it rotates LÖVE's OpenGL ES
buffer. This patch takes a suboptimal present as a success on Android,
and changes nothing else: VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR and a lost surface
still rebuild, as does any rebuild requested, and a rotation that changes
the window's size still rebuilds once, through backbufferChanged (lines
681-703). Acquiring an image already takes a suboptimal result as a
success (line 1472).

Nothing in Lota can do this: the swap chain, the present, and its result
are inside LÖVE's Graphics, which no binding reaches. CMake applies the
patch only when it builds the engine for Android, to a copy of the file
in the build tree (ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love is never
written to, and every other platform compiles LÖVE's own file.

On a device that runs LÖVE on Vulkan, in landscape, read the intervals
between presents (adb shell dumpsys SurfaceFlinger --latency with the
game's layer): they should be about 16.7 milliseconds, as in portrait and
as with OpenGL ES, where without the patch they alternate between 33 and
50. A OnePlus Nord N30 5G (Android 14, Adreno 619, Vulkan 1.1.128) showed that:
without the patch its intervals in landscape had a median of 50
milliseconds and alternated between 33 and 50, and with it the median was
16.7 and about a tenth of the frames were 33, against 1.4 to 2.1 percent
in portrait, which is probably the compositor's rotation of the identity
buffer; the image was upright and full screen.

Drop this patch when LÖVE no longer rebuilds its swap chain on
VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR, or if a device shows that it does not help.

diff -ruN a/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp b/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
--- a/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
@@ -640,6 +640,16 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
+#ifdef LOVE_ANDROID
+	// Android's loader returns VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR from every present while
+	// the window's transform hint differs from the swap chain's identity
+	// preTransform, as it does in landscape. A new swap chain would have
+	// the same preTransform and get the same result, so Lota's patch takes
+	// the present as a success (ext/lota/engine/vulkan_present.patch).
+	if (result == VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR)
+		result = VK_SUCCESS;
+#endif
+
 	if (result == VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR || result == VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR || result == VK_ERROR_SURFACE_LOST_KHR
 		|| swapChainRequestFlags != SWAP_CHAIN_REQUEST_KEEP)
 	{
